quiet.md #14: tell same-named fallback faces apart by glyph count

CoreText's fallback copy of PingFang SC (PingFangUI.ttc) and the PingFang SC
family in PingFang.ttc share the PostScript name PingFangSC-Regular but not
their glyph tables. id_for_native_font looked the fallback face up by name,
found the other copy, and Chinese text in the editor was drawn with the wrong
glyphs. Keep every face under its name and pick the one with the same glyph
count. The app checks this in editor::text::tests.

